Description: Shadowfetch Phoenix Recovery (safety pillar)
 Phoenix Recovery for Shadowfetch Linux 2.1.5 "Fire Edition". On a Btrfs
 root it arms snapper at first boot (so Debian snapper's shipped 80snapper
 apt hook wraps every dpkg run in pre/post Phoenix Points), keeps free
 space ahead of package transactions (79phoenix-space, sorted before
 80snapper), and restores any Point crash-atomically: snapshot-aside, then
 a single renameat2(RENAME_EXCHANGE) swap, so an @ subvolume exists at
 every instant and a power cut can never leave the machine unbootable.
 An interrupted restore is journalled by phase and is finished, or undone,
 on the next boot: phoenix-recover reads that journal and the volume itself,
 decides whether the exchange completed, repairs an external /boot staged
 for a generation that never landed, and collects previous roots and kernel
 backups under a bound.
 Restore is supported from inside the "Last Known Good Flame" read-only
 snapshot session. Also ships the user-scope Plasma desktop reset (personal
 files untouched, undoable by construction) and the privacy-safe recovery
 report exporter. Nothing here makes a network connection.
